    "datasource": "Kodak Bright Sun Film / GA, publication E-2328, July 2003; SHA256 fb723facbbad3bff66e663d590f30db7c7c22cfc3ff472c066495628a8fa1ef0. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-bright-sun-ga/recipe.json. Dye spectra: kodak_gold_200 shapes, scaled so their mixture reproduces this sheet's own midscale-neutral-minus-D-min. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Measured, not assumed: the sheet's D-min trace is the spectral base density, and what the Status M densitometer reads through it is subtracted from the characteristic curves. The first stock here whose base is not a flat guess. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_gold_200. Same class of stock. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [1.0244, 1.0204, 0.9178], log-exposure shift [0.0084, 0.0, -0.1659], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 20.2% before, 5.3% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
